<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30015" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγγύ-η</span></b>  (rarely <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγγύα</span></b> ; but <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἐγγύαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					11(2).226
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>A</u>
				29
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
			</span></i> (v. infr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				4.346
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>), ἡ: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν, γύαλον</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγγυαλίζω</span>):—<i>pledge put into one's
				hand</i>: generally, <i>surety, security</i>, whether
			received or given, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.351
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τιθέναι τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					898
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγγύας</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποτίνειν ὑπέρ τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					2.2.12
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐγγυᾶσθαι</span> (v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγγυάω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποδιδόναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					53.27
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ὁμολογεῖν</span>,
			= Lat. <i>vadimonium facere</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				11.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				455.3
			</span></i> (Epist. M. Antonii); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ἐ. τῆς ἐπὶ τὴν τράπεζαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					33.10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγγύας ἄτα ᾽στι θυγάτηρ, ἐγγύα δὲ
					ζαμίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					268
				</span></i>
			: prov., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγγύη, πάρα δ᾽ ἄτη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Chrm.</u>
					165a
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>betrothal</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				774e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ποιεῖσθαί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Is.
					3.28
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ.: σημεῖον ἐν θυτικῇ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ; ῡ</span> only in <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.366
			</span></i>.]</div>
